exports[`list pages > renders the index, sources and pricing both ways > calendars 1`] = `
"# Calendars

Zeitwide covers 2 calendars; dates outside a calendar's coverage are never guessed.

## Payment rails

Payment rails

| Calendar | Time zone | Weekend | Covered |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| [CHAPS has 3 closing days in 2026, 3 on weekdays](https://zeitwide.example/calendars/GB-CHAPS) | Europe/London | saturday, sunday | 1 January 2026 to 31 December 2027 |
| [FedNow has no closing days in 2026](https://zeitwide.example/calendars/US-FEDNOW) | Europe/London | None, open every day | Every date |

## Sources

Zeitwide release 2026.10.28.1.
"
`;

exports[`list pages > renders the index, sources and pricing both ways > pricing 1`] = `
"# Pricing

Zeitwide is free during the beta, with every feature included on every account.

The dataset is published under CC BY-NC 4.0, and the Python library with its local MCP server is MIT licensed.

## Free

- Every calendar: Fedwire, FedACH, FedNow, T2, CHAPS and public holidays
- REST API, hosted MCP server and change webhooks
- A signed receipt with every answer, and answers as of any past moment
- 10,000 API calls a day per key; 60 an hour without a key

## Open data and code

- [API keys are free from the developer quickstart](https://zeitwide.example/docs)

## Sources
"
`;

exports[`list pages > renders the index, sources and pricing both ways > sources 1`] = `
"# Sources

Zeitwide answers from 1 official source, listed here for closures in 2026 and 2027. A change is published only after two independent sources agree and a reviewer signs it off; this list is from release 2026.10.28.1.

## Sources

- GOV.UK: <https://www.gov.uk/bank-holidays> (Read 31 Oct 2026, 06:10 UTC). Backs CHAPS

Zeitwide release 2026.10.28.1.
"
`;

